    "notes": [
      "The circle has R = 169.0 ft as commercial program A prints it: only that radius ends exactly at its right endpoint (−15, 50); 169.1 dips 0.1 ft into the φ = 35° sand and raised every method by about 0.5 %. Program D's 2.254 (Bishop) and 2.258 (Spencer) were computed with R = 169.1 and are no longer checks. The three commercial program A models carry slightly different digitisations of the same dam. USACE 2.30; commercial program A GLE 2.309.",
      "An independent Bishop calculation on commercial program A's circle (R = 169.0 ft) gives 2.243, as cSlope does; commercial program A's 2.307 (Bishop and Spencer) is not explained and is not used as a check. Its Janbu corrected 2.290 carries the same offset (cSlope 2.248 matches an independent calculation to four digits, with the same f0 = 1.0568 as commercial program A's documented formula; its Janbu corrected / Bishop ratio 0.993 is not reproduced by any physical variant, which give 1.000–1.012); it stays as the problem's one program check, about 1.8 % above.",
      "cSlope fija options.tolerance = 0.001 (tolerancia del solver) en sus checks; no se importa: ogs usa analysis.tolerance = 1e-05.",
      "agua embalsada: la piezométrica pasa sobre el terreno; ogs la incluye en todas las versiones, con su peso y su empuje horizontal y sin sismo (F5.3); cSlope la carga con `followBoundary: false`."
